\import{fdip-macros}
\meta{agent-authored}{true}
\tag{fdip}
\taxon{Remark}
\title{The missing relation between frames and cell directions}
\date{2026-11-17}

\p{The cubical maps #{u_i\wedge} and #{u_i\cdot} in
the [rotation-only operator](fdip-00YO) use the fixed cell directions. The internal
exterior action changes coefficients in a separate factor.
No field relating these two sorts of directions, with a compatible
affine gauge law, has been declared. Such a relation is often
called frame or soldering data.}

\p{The edge-direction proposal fails linear conjugacy by
\ref{fdip-00YZ}; the rotation-only operator ignores every
translation label by \ref{fdip-00Z2}, even when torsion classes differ.
Whether a separately defined affine-sensitive operator has a
torsion-sensitive determinant remains open. These results neither
rule out affine matter in general nor supply frame dynamics or
select a spinor representation.}
